<BaseLayout title="SP6 (Sanyinjiao) — Three Yin Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate SP6 (Sanyinjiao) — the Three Yin Intersection point. Benefits include women's health, sleep support, and circulation improvement." articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">SP6 (Sanyinjiao) — Three Yin Intersection</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">SP6, known as Sanyinjiao or Three Yin Intersection, is the meeting point of three Yin meridians: Spleen, Liver, and Kidney. It is widely used for women's health, sleep, and circulation.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/sp6-location.png" alt="SP6 acupressure point location on the inner lower leg" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">SP6 is located on the inner lower leg, approximately 4 cun (four finger-widths) above the tip of the inner ankle, on the posterior border of the tibia (shinbone).</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Women's health:</strong> SP6 regulates the menstrual cycle, eases menstrual cramps, and supports reproductive health.</li>
      <li><strong>Insomnia:</strong> It promotes deep, restful sleep and is especially helpful for those who wake frequently during the night.</li>
      <li><strong>Circulation:</strong> SP6 improves circulation in the lower body and may ease cold feet and leg swelling.</li>
      <li><strong>Digestive health:</strong> It helps with bloating, gas, and poor appetite related to Spleen Qi deficiency.</li>
      <li><strong>Stress and mood:</strong> SP6 calms the mind and helps regulate mood swings associated with PMS.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage SP6</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Sit with your leg resting comfortably on a chair or sofa.</li>
      <li>Place your thumb on the SP6 point on one leg.</li>
      <li>Apply firm, steady pressure using small circular motions.</li>
      <li>Hold for 1— minutes before switching to the other leg.</li>
      <li>Repeat once or twice daily as needed.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2018 randomized controlled trial in <em>Journal of Integrative Medicine</em> found that SP6 acupressure significantly reduced primary dysmenorrhea pain compared to ibuprofen.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30236584/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>BMC Complementary Medicine and Therapies</em> showed that SP6 stimulation improved sleep quality in postmenopausal women.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32513465/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2021 study in <em>Medicine</em> demonstrated that SP6 acupressure reduced anxiety and cortisol levels in women undergoing gynecological surgery.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34114994/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Avoid during pregnancy:</strong> SP6 can stimulate uterine contractions and should be avoided during pregnancy.</li>
      <li>Do not massage over varicose veins, wounds, or rashes on the lower leg.</li>
      <li>Use gentle pressure if you have diabetes or poor circulation in the legs.</li>
      <li>Stop if you experience sharp or shooting pain.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">SP6 pairs well with <a href="/points/cv6-qihai-acupressure-point">CV6 (Qihai)</a> for women's health and with <a href="/points/ht7-shenmen-acupressure-point">HT7 (Shenmen)</a> for insomnia. For digestive issues, combine with <a href="/points/st36-zusanli-acupressure-point">ST36 (Zusanli)</a>.</p>
  </section></article>
